@id=declared-maturity-derived-stage @kind=decision
Feature: Maturity is declared and checked; that it works is derived

  Not one status field, which rots: how far a thing has come, up to implemented, the promise that
  it is built, is a judgement, so it is declared and checked against the content; that it works is
  read from scenario results and never declared. The price is that the check sees only the shape of
  the content, so a placeholder paragraph with a token scenario is ready, and that a spec is
  verified only in a checkout where its scenarios ran.
